\par\par \b \uc2 DJ MARKET TALK:  \highlight22\uc2 Colombia \highlight\uc2  Peso  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Successful So Far\b0\par\par\uc2 1,264 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 August 2012\par 15:46\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2012, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 9:46 EDT - Why ask others to do what you can do yourself? Colombia's government, after begging to no avail for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to increase its dollar purchases to weaken the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , started buying greenbacks on its own this week, at least $300M worth, and said to expect more of the same in the following weeks. This is $60M a day, far more than the $20M daily by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and it's worked well so far: COP is at 2-month high of 1,823 for a dollar, up 1.8% from its close at end of last week. (dan.molinski@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 9:35 EDT - With the 10-year yield, at 1.82%, back just below the start-of-year's 1.86%, "yields have normalized somewhat from emergency levels," says Dan Dektar at Smith Breeden. Just three weeks ago, it hit an all-time low of 1.38%. Still, Dektar calls current levels more of a safe-haven play than an investment proposition. His firm remains light on Treasurys; it's more willing to take on credit risk for better yield with high-grade corporates. (cynthia.lin@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 9:33 EDT - Whether it's uncertainty about Europe, fears about another \uc2 Knight Capital Group\uc2 -like (KCG) trading glitch or vacations to the beach, the summer doldrums are in full effect. On average, 4.35B shares have traded daily this week. Another session at those levels would put this week's total volume at the lowest so far this year, excluding weeks shortened by holidays. (matthew.jarzemsky@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 9:32 EDT - An encouraging sign for the sliding Treasury bond market -- foreign central banks have been buyers for the past two weeks, even as many other investors cashed out. The Fed's custody holdings data late yesterday show foreign central banks' Treasury bond holdings increased $8.4B in the latest week, following $9.5B addition in the previous week. "We continue to...see the [Treasury] market as a buy," says David Ader, head of US government-bond strategy at CRT. "We await our opportunity and proof, via the price action, that the call is a correct one." If the 10-year yield closes below 1.77%, Ader says it'll be a convincing signal to get into the market. The 10-year note recently 5/32 higher to yield 1.819%. (min.zeng@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 9:31 EDT - Brean Murray is no bull on Idenix's (IDIX) hepatitis C treatment, calling it "incapable of being the cornerstone of a competitive all-oral regimen" for the drug maker. But IDIX has another virus-treating drug in the pipeline that the investment bank considers more promising. So after Thursday's 29% stock slump after the FDA put a partial hold on clinical trials for the hep C drug, Brean Murray upgrades IDIX to hold while pulling its $6 price target. It's up 4.3% in early trading at $6.09 but has fallen 24% this week. (andrew.fitzgerald@dowjones.com; @drewfitzgerald)\par \par \uc2 9:28 EDT - Prepare to sift through some fancy branding campaigns along with deluge of information when hedge funds are allowed more leeway to advertise. PR firm Walek & Associates says many funds are quietly preparing to make more information publicly available on their web site and build a media profile. Firm says branding matters because investors also look at "visibility differentiation and credibility" on top of performance. Adds branding doesn't necessarily mean performance: None of the billion dollar money raisers last year were found to be on the year's top performer lists. The SEC will meet on Aug 22 on the matter. (amy.or@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 9:17 EDT - The Chilean peso trades nearly unchanged against the dollar after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  held the interest rate at 5% for the seventh consecutive month, as expected. Some market participants expected the bank would raise the curtain for a possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but it only said "the peso has appreciated." Peso recently trading at CLP483.00 versus Thursday's close of CLP482.80, according to Valor Futuro newswire. (graciela.ibanez@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 9:13 EDT - Increases of the number of US Krispy Kreme (KKD) stores, including the first for company-owned ones in 7 years, and "already industry-leading international growth could result in sustained high-teens to low-20% EPS growth and an expanded valuation," says Wedbush as it starts coverage of the restaurant chain at outperform and sets a $9 price target. The investment bank sees international earnings more than doubling within 5 years. That as July's efforts around KKD's 75th anniversary "could have resulted in 'best month in years', as some stores put it." Shares are up 2% premarket at $6.68. (kevin.kingsbury@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 9:03 EDT - "The \uc2 Bank of Canada\uc2 's tightening bias is increasingly looking untenable," National Bank's Krishen Rangasamy says after July's softer inflation report. Total inflation rate is now tracking 1.00% in Q3, Rangasamy says, short of the \uc2 Bank of Canada\uc2 's estimated for 1.2% for the quarter. The core rate, meanwhile, is tracking 1.2%, significantly lower than BOC's 1.9% estimate. The Canadian dollar is shrugging off the report, even trimming some losses in the wake of it, with the US dollar now at C$0.9883, from C$0.9866 late Thursday. (karen.johnson@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 9:01 EDT - A Peruvian delegation has arrived in Venezuela, and the countries are expected to finalize a new accord replacing trade pacts that lapsed when Venezuela withdrew from the regional customs union of the \uc2 Andean Community of Nations\uc2  in April 2011. Venezuela completed its long-pending exit with only temporary accords in place with Colombia and Peru. Current CAN members also include Bolivia and Ecuador. (ezequiel.minaya@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 8:58 EDT - \uc2 Morgan Stanley\uc2  says WellPoint (WLP) could face more pressure from an unfavorable mix of commercial health-insurance prices and medical costs as it downgrades WLP to equal-weight and says the company's "risk-reward looks less compelling" than peers. WLP cut its 2012 guidance during last month, mainly citing faster-than-expected erosion in its membership ranks, and shares have fallen 5.8% since. But \uc2 Morgan Stanley\uc2  sees more problems afoot than membership levels and cites "concern that poor cost-trend visibility has led to a mispricing of the commercial book." WLP, inactive premarket, has rebounded 8.6% this month. (jon.kamp@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 8:57 EDT - As emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  lose ground to the dollar, \uc2 Morgan Stanley\uc2  recommends that investors buy some of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  at these cheaper rates. "We continue to believe we are in a risk-positive environment," the analysts said. They recommend going long the Russian ruble on the expectation that Russia will hike rates, giving investors a chance to get higher carry. Long the Mexican peso vs the yen, on the stronger growth prospects of the Latin American country. USD/MXN is up today at 13.2113 as is the USD/RUB at 31.926, according to CQG data. (prabha.natarajan@dowjones.com) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par To contact the Market Talk Editors, \par Bradley Davis, 212 416-2654, bradley.davis@dowjones.com \par Kevin Kingsbury, 212 416-2354, kevin.kingsbury@dowjones.com \par John Shipman, 212 416-2181,john.shipman@dowjones.com \par Patrick Sullivan, 212 416-2326,Patrick.sullivan@dowjones.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 August 17, 2012 09:46 ET (13:46 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020120817e88h003vu\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw200\pich25\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3000\pichgoal375
