\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Colombia Central Bank \highlight\uc2  July  \highlight22\uc2 Forex Intervention \highlight\uc2  Was $400 Million\b0\par\par\uc2 176 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 August 2012\par 22:17\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 BOGOTA--The \uc2 Colombian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said Monday it had purchased $400 million in the spot market in July under its policy of buying at least $20 million a day to drain U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and build up international reserves.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's dollar purchases in the spot market are aimed at preventing excessive strength in the peso. The bank has bought $2.36 billion this year and has pledged to continue the daily purchases through at least Nov. 4.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  used a similar strategy in 2011, when it purchased $3.72 billion until October, then ended its policy of daily purchases as fears over the European debt crisis caused the peso to weaken on its own, rendering such \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  unnecessary.\par \par \uc2 The Colombian peso weakened slightly agains the dollar Monday to close at COP1,788.50 to the dollar, from COP1,786.00 a day earlier.\par \par \uc2 Write to Darcy Crowe at darcy.crowe@dowjones.com. [ 06-08-12 2017GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020120806e88600153\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
