\par\par \b \uc2 DJ Foreign Investment Into Colombia Surges in First Half of Year\b0\par\par\uc2 324 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Juli 2012\par 17:35\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2012, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 BOGOTA--Foreign direct investment into Colombia surged in the first half of this year, the latest indication that the peso's strength against the dollar is being driven by flows of the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  into this Andean nation.\par \par \uc2 Preliminary data released Monday by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  shows that foreign direct investment into Colombia jumped to US$9.38 billion in the first six months of 2012, up 26% from the year-earlier period.\par \par \uc2 The surge in foreign direct investment, which is largely geared at Colombia's oil and mining industries, is commonly cited by analysts as one of the key factors behind the peso's strength against the dollar. The peso has appreciated more than 7% so far this year and ranks as one of the world's best-performing \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 On Monday, the peso traded at COP1,777.2 after closing at COP1,776.60 on Friday.\par \par \uc2 Despite recurrent calls from exporters for the government to curb the peso's strength, \b \highlight22\uc2 Colombia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market consists of having the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  buy at least $20 million daily in the spot market, a move designed to mop up excess dollar liquidity.\par \par \uc2 Over the course of this year, the bank has bought $1.96 billion, and it has vowed to continue the daily purchases through at least Nov. 4.\par \par \uc2 The government has called for a more aggressive \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  while also steering away from implementing capital controls, which limit foreign investment.\par \par \uc2 The trading volumes in the spot market can easily reach about $1 billion daily, leading many analysts to project that even if the bank steps up its dollar purchases, it will not be able to reverse the peso's appreciation.\par \par \uc2 Write to Darcy Crowe at darcy.crowe@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 July 16, 2012 11:35 ET (15:35 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020120716e87g004i9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
