\par\par \b \uc2 POLL-Colombia cenbank seen holding rates steady on Fri\b0\par\par\uc2 716 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Juni 2012\par 17:23\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Policymakers to decide interest rate on Friday\par \par \uc2 * Most analysts see rate at 5.25 pct through 2012\par \par \uc2 By Nelson Bocanegra\par \par \uc2 BOGOTA, June 25 (Reuters) - Colombia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is seen keeping its benchmark interest rate unchanged at its policy meeting on Friday as inflation expectations remain contained and worries over the European economic crisis ease, according to the unanimous view of 30 analysts polled by Reuters.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  has held the rate steady since March at 5.25 percent to provide economic stimulus amid concerns that weakness in the global economy could spill into Colombia.\par \par \uc2 The bank has raised borrowing costs 225 basis points since early last year to prevent Latin America's No. 4 economy from overheating and ease bank lending over fears that households are becoming too indebted.\par \par \uc2 The majority of the 30 analysts, based in Colombia and on Wall Street, c onsulted by Reuters thought the bank would keep the rate unchanged for the rest of 2012.\par \par \uc2 The number of analysts who expected the bank to raise rates again this year to cool the pace of consumer lending have gone down while more now believed that a rate cut could be on the table in the coming months.\par \par \uc2 Economic figures in the first quarter and in April come in stark contrast to 2011 when Colombia's full-year gross domestic product grew at its highest level in four years.\par \par \uc2 In the first quarter of 2012, the economy grew at its slowest rate in more than a year as last year's rate hikes took effect and the mining sector was weakened by lower commodities prices and renewed attacks by rebel groups.\par \par \uc2 The economy grew 0.3 percent in the first quarter versus 1.2 percent in the previous three months - the slowest quarterly growth rate since the third quarter of 2010.\par \par \uc2 Since Colombia's last policy meeting at the end of May, worries that Greece might leave the eurozone have subsided after elections that brought a conservative-led government to power.\par \par \uc2 "April activity numbers were negative, but we think still not bad enough so as to sway the majority of the board, some of whom remain concerned about credit growth, to act by loosening monetary policy," Bank Of America \uc2 Merrill Lynch\uc2  said in a note.\par \par \uc2 "We expect (the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) to remain on hold. Although the minutes showed significant concerns about the global economy, concerns about a slowdown have somewhat diminished relative to the moment at which the last meeting was held, given the outcome of the Greek elections."\par \par \uc2 Colombia's slow economic growth in the first quarter and a fall in industrial production and retail sales in April showed that the economy was nearing its potential, according to one of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's seven board members.\par \par \uc2 Monetary policy is determined by the seven-member central board, which meets monthly.\par \par \uc2 Some board members have said that the authority could adopt a countercyclical monetary policy if there were a significant deterioration in Europe.\par \par \uc2 Colombian policymakers are concerned that continued credit expansion is pressuring consumer prices even though inflation has remained relatively steady in recent months.\par \par \uc2 Consumer prices rose 3.44 percent during the 12-month period through May, slightly above the 3 percent midpoint of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's 2- to 4-percent annual target range.\par \par \uc2 The majority of analysts ruled out additional measures to stem the rising peso \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which is the strongest gainer among the world's 36 most-traded \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Two experts polled by Reuters, however, believed the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would increase the amount of dollars it is purchasing at auction from the current $20 million or more daily - the peso has firmed 7.7 percent so far this year.\par \par \uc2 Finance Minister Juan Carlos Echeverry, a board member, has said he favored more aggressive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  into the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to stem the peso.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Colombia\b0 \highlight\uc2  has become one of the best performing economies in Latin America and attracted a flood of foreign investment, mainly into the oil and mining sectors.\par \par \uc2 Last year the country was granted an investment grade credit rating from Fitch, \uc2 Moody's\uc2  and \uc2 Standard & Poor's\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 (Writing by Jack Kimball Editing by W Simon)\par \par \uc2 COLOMBIA-RATES/ (POLL) | ABN | E | RBN | M | D | NAT   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020120628e86p0011h\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw427\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal6405\pichgoal600
