\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Market  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  and Debt Gain Modestly\b0\par\par\uc2 By Prabha Natarajan   \par \uc2 612 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Juni 2012\par 22:43\par \uc2 Dow Jones News Service\par \uc2 DJ\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 Emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and debt were a tad improved Friday, riding on hopes that central banks would ride to the rescue or Greece's pro-Europe party would take the lead in Sunday's election.\par \par \uc2 Emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are on the cusp of what could be a hefty market rally. The May selloff of these \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  has brought most of them to levels investors find attractive and reasonable.\par \par \uc2 "A lot of these \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  don't look fundamentally overvalued, as they had, and are becoming a more attractive investment," said Keith Brakebill, a portfolio manager at \uc2 Russell Investments\uc2 . While the fund is long on emerging markets, it also has instituted a proxy hedge with a basket of developed-market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , such as the Canadian dollar, Australian dollar and the euro against the dollar.\par \par \uc2 His Russell Global Opportunistic Credit Fund (RGCAX), with $853 million in assets, also began buying U.S. high-yield and high-quality emerging-market dollar and local-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bonds in May, once it was clear there would be another election in Greece. His reasoning is that if markets recover after the election, these two asset classes would provide high returns. However, if markets sell off, these bonds could be traded to raise liquidity and seek investments in other distressed opportunities.\par \par \uc2 Like him, many other investors returned to emerging markets in the latest week, according to data from EPFR Global. Net capital flows to emerging-market bond funds totaled $361 million, reversing three weeks of outflows.\par \par \uc2 But many other investors are on hold, worried that an unfavorable result in Greece could trigger another selloff, and prefer a larger-than-usual dose of cash.\par \par \uc2 The rally in equities Friday is another instance of investors getting overly optimistic without reason, cautions Jamie Stuttard, portfolio manager of the \uc2 Fidelity International\uc2  Bond Fund (FINUX) with $394 million in assets. He says investors expect coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  action and some more direction from the spate of policy meetings next week.\par \par \uc2 "It's another cycle of rescue versus reality," he said. The reality is Spanish bond yields are near 7%, and there is another bond auction next week that the beleaguered European sovereign has to clear.\par \par \uc2 "Portfolios should be pretty liquid in the current environment, and cash is healthy," he said.\par \par \uc2 In addition, he has been buying up options to hedge out risk of an extreme situation like the euro collapsing on Monday.\par \par \uc2 Others such as Nomura's trading desk, protectively, have gone long on the dollar, because there is only upside against the \b \highlight22\uc2 Colombia\b0 \highlight\uc2  peso. \b \highlight22\uc2 Colombia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's aggressive verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has helped keep the dollar above 1,783 Colombian pesos, giving the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  a break from its continued appreciation versus the dollar. If the weekend brought a positive outcome in Greece, the dollar's weakening beyond COP1,760 would be curbed by Colombia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . If Greece's elections results were unfavorable, the dollar would gain. Currently, the dollar is trading at COP1,784.70, down 0.31% on the day, according to CQG data.\par \par \uc2 The Brazilian real also is gaining on the dollar. Investors have taken note of the country's indication that it may backtrack on some of its more aggressive moves to depreciate the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and see this as an opportune time to buy the real. The dollar, currently, is trading at BRL2.0441, down 0.57% on the day.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, emerging market debt was trading five basis points narrower at 386 basis points over comparable Treasury yields on the \uc2 J.P. Morgan\uc2  Emerging Markets Bond Index Global.\par \par \uc2 Write to Prabha Natarajan at prabha.natarajan@dowjones.com [ 06-15-12 1643ET ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJ00000020120615e86f0013h\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
