\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging-Market  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2 , Debt Rally on Hopes of Coordinated Action\b0\par\par\uc2 By Prabha Natarajan   \par \uc2 469 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Juni 2012\par 23:15\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 Emerging-market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and debt were eerily calm most of Thursday as investors hunkered down ahead of Greece's elections on Sunday.\par \par \uc2 A late-afternoon report of global coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 central-bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  action helped lead a mild rally in these \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , though market participants wondered about the endurance of such a move.\par \par \uc2 For most of the day, though, investors preferred dollars and stayed out of making any major moves. Earlier in the day, Brazil's backtracking on some of its aggressive taxes on foreign loans elicited little reaction from the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 One trader called it a case of "too little, too late." However, late in the day, as other higher-yielding assets rallied, the real also found its legs. The dollar was trading at BRL2.0574, down from its earlier high of BRL2.0770, according to CQG data.\par \par \uc2 Other proxies for emerging-market risk, such as the Mexican peso and the Chilean peso, made a strong late-afternoon recovery, too. The dollar, against the Mexican peso, slipped below MXN14, to trade at MXN13.9050, down nearly 0.9% on the day. Similarly, the dollar was more than 1% weaker against the Chilean peso at CLP498.20, according to CQG data.\par \par \uc2 The only commonly traded Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buck the trend was the \b \highlight22\uc2 Colombia\b0 \highlight\uc2  peso on \b \highlight22\uc2 central-bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . On Thursday, \b \highlight22\uc2 Colombia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's finance minister renewed calls for "aggressive" \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb the peso's volatility. Such a move may halt the appreciation, but it won't weaken the peso, said David Rees, an emerging-market economist at Capital Economics.\par \par \uc2 The dollar is down 10% against the peso for the year, making it the best performing emerging-market \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  this year. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been buying dollars daily to weaken the peso. But continued flows of foreign-direct investments into Colombia, its exports to the U.S. and stable commodity prices have made Colombia resilient. CapEcon expects the dollar to stick around the COP1750 range on \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  from its current level of COP1790.20, according to CQG data.\par \par \uc2 Elsewhere, emerging Europe remained hardy. The Hungarian forint, Czech koruna and Polish zloty were all up against the euro, and showed little signs of stress during the course of trading.\par \par \uc2 There was no sign of stress in local-debt markets of emerging economies, with foreign holdings of the bonds resilient despite the broader weakness globally, said Benoit Anne, head of emerging-markets strategy at \uc2 Societe Generale\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, emerging-market debt was stronger by eight basis points on the \uc2 J.P. Morgan\uc2  Emerging Markets Bond Index-Global, at 386 basis points over comparable Treasury yields. Emerging-market issuers continued to stay out of the market.\par \par \uc2 Write to Prabha Natarajan at prabha.natarajan@dowjones.com. [ 14-06-12 2115GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020120614e86e0014c\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
