\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Colombia \highlight\uc2  Finance Minister Renews Call for Aggressive Peso  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 358 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Juni 2012\par 18:13\par \uc2 Dow Jones News Service\par \uc2 DJ\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 BOGOTA--Colombian Finance Minister Juan Carlos Echeverry renewed calls for a more "aggressive" \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, a measure that could help curb sharp volatility in the peso.\par \par \uc2 Echeverry said Thursday he is advocating a "more aggressive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 " by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which has been buying U.S. dollars at a rate of about $20 million daily in the spot market. The finance minister is one of the seven members in the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's board of directors.\par \par \uc2 "I'm seeing jobs at risk" because of the peso's appreciation, Echeverry said Thursday during a presentation. The peso has appreciated sharply against the dollar this year and has suffered bouts of sharp volatility.\par \par \uc2 On Thursday the peso trades at COP1,788 after closing at COP1,784.90 a day earlier. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy consists of buying at least $20 million daily in the spot market, a move designed to mop up excess dollar liquidity.\par \par \uc2 Over the course of this year, the bank has bought $1.58 billion, and it has vowed to continue the daily purchases through at least Nov. 4.\par \par \uc2 Echeverry in the past has called for a more aggressive \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  while also steering away from implementing capital controls, which limit foreign investment.\par \par \uc2 The finance minister said Thursday the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could increase its dollar purchases without spawning faster inflation, which the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would like to see end the year at around 3%. He added that intensifying the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's purchases could help limit some of the volatility in the exchange rate.\par \par \uc2 The trading volumes in the spot market can easily reach around $1 billion daily, leading many analysts to project that even if the bank steps up its dollar purchases it will not be able to reverse the peso's appreciation.\par \par \uc2 Capital Economics, a London research firm, said in a report "we doubt that the authorities will succeed in significantly weakening the peso."\par \par \uc2 Write to Darcy Crowe at darcy.crowe@dowjones.com. [ 06-14-12 1213ET ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJ00000020120614e86e000do\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
