\par\par \b \uc2 Colombia Stocks Rise On Higher Oil Prices; Peso Treads Water\b0\par\par\uc2 245 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 April 2012\par 22:58\par \uc2 Dow Jones Business News\par \uc2 DJON\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 --Colombia stocks gain for second session, led by higher prices in oil shares\par \par \uc2 --Shares of state oil company \uc2 Ecopetrol\uc2  gained 1.7% to 5,510 pesos\par \par \uc2 --Peso ends virtually unchanged at COP1,762.20 per dollar\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Dan Molinski \par    Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 BOGOTA -(Dow Jones)- Colombian stocks climbed Thursday, driven by a rise in global prices for oil that pushed up heavily traded shares of oil firms \f28 \uc2 \f2 Ecopetrol\f28 \uc2 \f2  (ECOPETROL.BO, EC) and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Pacific Rubiales\f28 \uc2 \f2  (PRE.T, PREC.BO).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Colcap, which is the Colombian Stock Exchange's benchmark index, climbed 0.58% to end at 1,759.62 points.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Shares of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Ecopetrol\f28 \uc2 \f2  rose 1.7% to COP5,510, while Canada-based Rubiales shares also gained 1.7%, ending at COP50,960.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Meanwhile, the Colombian peso ended virtually unchanged at COP1,762.20 per dollar from COP1,761.85 a day earlier, according to Set-\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The peso is 9% stronger against the dollar this year due to a record amount of foreign direct investment. Some analysts believe \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Colombia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will announce new \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  plans Monday to prevent further strength in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The yield on Colombia's peso-denominated bond due July 2024 closed at 7.099% after beginning the session at 7.017%. Yields have been declining due to lower inflation data.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Dan Molinski, Dow Jones Newswires; 57-310-867-6542; dan.molinski@dowjones.com [ 04-26-12 1658ET ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJON000020120426e84q000b7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
