\par\par \b \uc2 *DJ Colombia  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  President: Global Economy In Line With Outlook\b0\par\par\uc2 639 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 April 2012\par 22:56\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2012, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 20 Apr 2012 16:57 EDT *DJ  Colombia's Uribe: Global Uncertainty Remains High, But Lower Than Before\par \par \uc2 20 Apr 2012 16:57 EDT *DJ  Colombia's Uribe: Colombia Growth, Inflation 'Exactly' On Course\par \par \uc2 20 Apr 2012 16:57 EDT *DJ  Colombia's Uribe: Economy Would Benefit From Weaker \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 20 Apr 2012 16:57 EDT *DJ  \b \highlight22\uc2 Colombia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Uribe: \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Will \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  When Benefits Outweigh Costs\par \par \uc2 20 Apr 2012 16:58 EDT DJ  Colombia \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President: Global Economy In Line With Outlook\par \par \uc2 -- Colombia \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sees global, domestic outlook playing out as expected\par \par \uc2 -- \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor sees growth this year at 5%, inflation at 3%\par \par \uc2 -- \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  always ready to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market when benefits outweigh costs \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Matthew Cowley \par    Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 WASHINGTON (Dow Jones)--The global growth outlook remains largely in line with the Colombian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's outlook, although oil prices are slightly higher, and domestic growth and inflation are also on course, the president of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , Jose Dario Uribe, said Friday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "In the global situation, levels of uncertainty are high but lower than they were," Uribe said in an interview on the sidelines of the spring meetings of the \f28 \uc2 \f2 International Monetary Fund\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Recent data "goes in the direction of what we had as the basic scenario" from the last quarter of last year, although oil prices are "a little bit higher" than the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  had expected, Uribe said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The higher oil prices are driving up Colombia's trade surplus, which may be the highest in many years, he added.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Growth will probably be slightly negative in Europe, with a decline in gross domestic product of around 0.5%, while the U.S. could grow between 1.5% and 2%, he said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Colombian economy, meanwhile, is also responding to the series of interest rate hikes made last year and earlier this year.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "All the information we have now suggest that growth will be around 5% and inflation is around 3%, which is exactly where we want to be," Uribe said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Uribe said that changes in interest rates have an almost immediate and significant impact on the market's inflation expectations, which are currently around 3%, as well as market interest rates. The final impact of interest rates can be a lag of between nine and 18 months, he said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Colombia's benchmark rate stands at 5.25%.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Meanwhile, Uribe said that the country's free-floating \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  remains the best option for Colombia, and helps the country absorb shocks such as the increase in terms of trade.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Yet, he said, "as we've been saying for some time, it would be appropriate for the Colombian economy to have a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  that is less appreciated."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The official said efforts by the government to save some of the revenues from oil exports are crucial in terms of reducing the impact on the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has continued to build foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves, "and at some moments when we've seen that the behavior of the exchange rate appeared to have some speculative aspects, where there's been a misalignment, that has also motivated us on some occasions to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is always prepared to act in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets when benefits of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  outweigh the costs, Uribe said. The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has in the past required a deposit on foreign borrowing, and that could be used again, he said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The bank currently buys $20 million daily in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market to prevent excessive peso gains, and is committed to continue doing this at least until early August.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Matthew Cowley, Dow Jones Newswires; +55 11 3544 7082; matthew.cowley@dowjones.com\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 April 20, 2012 16:58 ET (20:58 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020120420e84k006cn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
