\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 3-Colombia rate hike cycle may not be over - minutes\b0\par\par\uc2 633 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 April 2012\par 17:18\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Some board members say "adjustments" may be needed\par \par \uc2 * Continued credit expansion could pressure prices\par \par \uc2 * Q1 growth seen robust after Q4 slowdown\par \par \uc2 (Adds analyst quote, details on global situation)\par \par \uc2 By Nelson Bocanegra and Brian Ellsworth\par \par \uc2 BOGOTA, April 4 (Reuters) - Colombia's cycle of interest rate hikes may not be over despite a pause in March, after several \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  board members noted that "additional adjustments" to monetary policy may be needed, according to minutes published on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 The seven-member board voted unanimously in the March 23 meeting to leave the benchmark lending rate unchanged at 5.25 percent following a year-long, 225-basis-point rise that has helped cool inflation in one of Latin America's fastest-growing economies.\par \par \uc2 The minutes signaled concern among Colombian policymakers that a continued credit expansion may be pressuring consumer prices even though inflation has decelerated and tighter monetary policy helped slow growth in the fourth quarter.\par \par \uc2 "Given the data now at hand, and even considering the recent trend in inflation, several board members noted that inflationary pressures continue to weigh on the (balance of risks), which means additional adjustments in monetary policy might be necessary," the minutes read.\par \par \uc2 Other board members noted that "the neutral range of the bank's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate has been achieved already."\par \par \uc2 Inflation slowed in February to 0.61 percent from 0.73 percent in January.\par \par \uc2 Though growth in the fourth quarter was the slowest in a year at 1.3 percent, compared to 5.9 percent for all of 2011, the bank noted that first-quarter expansion appeared robust, providing further justification for \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  hawks.\par \par \uc2 "With respect to the economic situation in the first quarter of 2012, the figures on hand point to good performance," the minutes said. "Household consumption continues to be favored by consumer confidence, which is relatively high, despite the decline witnessed in February."\par \par \uc2 The bank also noted there has been no sign that "contagion" from the crisis in Europe and slower world economic growth is affecting Colombia, adding that exports continued to grow firmly while foreign direct investment remains strong.\par \par \uc2 RESERVE REQUIREMENTS\par \par \uc2 Changes to monetary policy could include "macro-prudential measures," which are meant to restrict liquidity and combat inflation without raising interest rates.\par \par \uc2 One \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  member requested the creation of a "reserve requirement for consumer lending."\par \par \uc2 This would likely require banks to set aside a percentage of all new consumer loans, according to one expert consulted by Reuters, in contrast to broader reserve requirements in which banks must leave a percentage of deposits with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Policymakers have raised concerns in recent months about the risks of Colombia's growing middle class taking on too much bank debt to buy new cars, real estate and home appliances.\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is still somewhat uncomfortable with the overall exuberant pace of demand ... rapid consumer credit growth, and low level of nominal and real rates," \uc2 Goldman Sachs\uc2  analyst Alberto Ramos said in a research note.\par \par \uc2 Higher interest rates make the peso more attractive to investors given near-zero yields in the United States and Europe. It has rallied nearly 9 percent since the start of the year.\par \par \uc2 Though Colombia has been largely shielded from the global downturn, industry leaders including coffee and banana growers have complained that a stronger \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  makes their exports less competitive in global markets.\par \par \uc2 The minutes made no mention of measures to stem the strengthening \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Finance Minister Juan Carlos Echeverry said in a recent interview with local media that \b \highlight22\uc2 Colombia\b0 \highlight\uc2  is considering "aggressive" \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prevent the peso from appreciating further.\par \par \uc2 (Editing by Helen Murphy, Chizu Nomiyama, Gary Crosse and James Dalgleish)\par \par \uc2 COLOMBIA-CENBANK/ (UPDATE 3) | ABN | D | M | NAT | E | RBN | U | RNP | DNP | PTD   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020120404e8440012d\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
