\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK: New Line In The Sand For  \highlight22\uc2 Colombia \highlight\uc2  Peso?\b0\par\par\uc2 143 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2012\par 14:42\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 8:42 (Dow Jones) Verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 forex intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  means different things to different people, but \b \highlight22\uc2 Colombia\b0 \highlight\uc2  Finance Minister Juan Carlos Echeverry's comments this week fit most any definition. He says the government is "now in favor of a more intense, more aggressive" \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the peso, which closed Thursday at COP1,792/dollar. Colombia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been buying $20M/day in the spot market to mop up excess dollars. Analysts were figuring more \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  might happen at the COP1,750 level, but RBS says COP1,800 could become the new line in the sand. The peso has gained 9% in 2012, but has fallen 2% since Echeverry spoke. (dan.molinski@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 Call us at (212) 416-2354 or email kevin.kingsbury@dowjones.com [ 30-03-12 1242GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1085   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020120330e83u0010p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
