\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Colombia \highlight\uc2  wants 'aggressive' peso  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 -report\b0\par\par\uc2 411 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2012\par 16:59\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Peso rising more than any major LatAm \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has dollar purchase program in place\par \par \uc2 BOGOTA, March 26 (Reuters) - Colombia wants to see more "aggressive" action to help stem gains in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and will ask the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to consider stepping up dollar purchases, Finance Minister Juan Carlos Echeverry said in an interview published on Monday.\par \par \uc2 Echeverry told \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  board members ahead of a policy meeting last Friday that President Juan Manuel Santos prefers a "model that requires much more \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the exchange rate," Colombian daily newspaper El Tiempo reported.\par \par \uc2 Colombia has seen record foreign investment flows as security improvements lowered the risk of exploring for oil, coal and other natural resources.\par \par \uc2 The flood of money, coupled with attractive yields compared with near-zero interest rates in developed nations, has bolstered the value of the peso.\par \par \uc2 "We have been in agreement with the amount of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and with the instruments we've used. Now we are inclined toward a more aggressive strategy, more intense, deeper," Echeverry said. "The bank has the muscle."\par \par \uc2 The bank said it has a dollar purchase program underway of "at least" $20 million a day that runs "at least" through Aug. 4 to help ease the rise of the peso. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has strengthened 9.4 percent this year, the most among major Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The government has also maintained funds from the sale of bonds and dividends from state oil company \uc2 Ecopetrol\uc2  overseas to prevent a flood of dollars entering the country.\par \par \uc2 Echeverry, who represents the government on the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's board, joined three other members who have expressed concern about the level of the peso, which on Monday opened at 1,758 per dollar.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  held the benchmark lending rate at 5.25 percent at its policy meeting last week, a move that could help slow pressure on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  following nine rate hikes of 225 basis points in just over a year.\par \par \uc2 Santos has faced pressure from exporters to ease \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  gains. Banana, coffee and flower growers have complained that high interest rates boost the peso, which dulls their competitive edge for goods sold abroad.\par \par \uc2 A decade-long U.S.-backed security crackdown has severely weakened Marxist FARC rebels, spurring business and consumer confidence and attracting almost $15 billion in foreign investment last year.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Helen Murphy; editing by Jeffrey Benkoe)\par \par \uc2 COLOMBIA-PESO | ABN | D | M   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020120326e83q00101\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
