\par\par \b \uc2 Colombia Stocks Surge 1.65%; Peso Hits 8-Month High\b0\par\par\uc2 320 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2012\par 22:18\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 --Colombian stocks hit nine-month high; peso reaches strongest in eight months\par \par \uc2 --\uc2 Ecopetrol\uc2  shares jump 3.5% to COP5,300\par \par \uc2 --Yields on Colombia peso bonds decline on reduced inflation fears\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Dan Molinski \par    Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 BOGOTA (Dow Jones)--Colombian stocks soared to a nine-month high Tuesday in line with fast-rising U.S. markets, while the peso reached its strongest level since July.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Colcap index, the benchmark for the Colombian Stock Exchange, climbed 1.7% to end at 1,747.23 points, its highest closing level since June 10. The index has risen 11% in 2012, erasing most of 2011's 14% decline.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The global rally that Colombia latched on to began after the release of strong U.S. data on retail sales and small-business optimism. And investors were encouraged even more on positive stress-test results from large U.S. banks.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The most heavily traded stocks in Bogota's bourse all showed impressive gains. National oil company \f28 \uc2 \f2 Ecopetrol\f28 \uc2 \f2  (ECOPETROL.BO, EC, ECP.T) rose 3.5% to COP5,300 while private oil producer \f28 \uc2 \f2 Pacific Rubiales\f28 \uc2 \f2  (PRE.T, PEGFF) climbed 1.6% to COP54,700. Bancolombia (PFBCOLOM.BO, CIB), the country's largest lender, rose 2.3% to COP28,840.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Meanwhile, the Colombian peso closed stronger at COP1,758.50 for a dollar, from COP1,763.65 a day earlier, according to Set-\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . Tuesday's closing level was the strongest since late July and could lead the country's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to consider more aggressive \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to prevent further \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  gains.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The yield on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Colombia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's peso-denominated bond due July 2024 closed at 7.190%, after beginning the session at 7.209%. Lower inflation expectations have been pushing down yields for several days.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Dan Molinski, Dow Jones Newswires; 57-310-867-6542; dan.molinski@dowjones.com\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  -0- \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 13-03-12 2118GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020120313e83d0018m\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw427\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal6405\pichgoal600
