\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Colombia \highlight\uc2 's Peso Touches Six-Month High Despite  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 296 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Februar 2012\par 15:16\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 BOGOTA (\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 )--\b \highlight22\uc2 Colombia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's peso is trading at a six-month high Monday morning despite persistent efforts by the government and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  over the past few weeks to stem the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's gains.\par \par \uc2 Cautious expectations of another Greek bailout are propelling investors to add to their emerging markets bets, pushing Colombia's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to COP1,773, its strongest level since mid August, and 0.6% stronger from Friday's close.\par \par \uc2 On Feb. 3, Colombia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it would start buying $20 million daily in the spot \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to help soak up excess U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  that's been flowing into the country's booming oil and coal sectors. The bank wants to weaken the peso because it is making Colombia's exported products less competitive.\par \par \uc2 For its part, Colombia's government said it would hold off on repatriating $1 billion worth of oil profits this year, which it hopes will also help stem the peso's gains.\par \par \uc2 While these measures have modestly slowed the pace of the peso's gains, analysts say the dollar flow toward Colombia from foreign investment is probably too great to halt or reverse the trend.\par \par \uc2 The peso's recent gains are also related to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's decision last month to increase its benchmark interest rate to 5.0%, citing the need to cool down a surging economy and inflationary pressures. So-called carry traders in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market are taking advantage of the higher rate to borrow \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  such as the dollar at payback rates near zero to buy the peso and pick up easy yields.\par \par \uc2 -By Dan Molinski, \uc2 Dow Jones Newswires\uc2 ; 57-310-867-6542; dan.molinski@dowjones.com [ 20-02-12 1416GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020120220e82k000qm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
