\par\par \b \uc2 CORRECTED- \highlight22\uc2 Colombia \highlight\uc2 's peso falls after cenbank  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 609 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Februar 2012\par 18:10\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Corrects level of peso)\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Colombia central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  ends dollar option auctions\par \par \uc2 * Re-starts buying at least $20 mln daily\par \par \uc2 * Exporters suffer from strong peso \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 By Helen Murphy\par \par \uc2 BOGOTA, Feb 6 (Reuters) - The Colombian peso weakened on Monday after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  resumed its dollar purchasing program to curb gains in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  that has prompted complaints from exporters.\par \par \uc2 The bank resumed buying at least $20 million daily for three months or more to boost reserves and slow gains in the peso. It also ended on Monday a plan to buy dollar options whenever the peso moved 4 percent or more from the 20-day moving average.\par \par \uc2 In \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading, the Colombian peso eased 0.15 percent to 1,787.00 pesos per dollar on Monday, but it has strengthened more than 8 percent so far this year.\par \par \uc2 The bank \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  followed moves by some regional central banks to stem the rise in their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Friday entered its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, buying dollar forwards.\par \par \uc2 "The latest set of measures announced by Colombia and Brazil to curb \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strength are unlikely to have a lasting impact on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets," said Capital Economics in a report. "Instead, fiscal reforms hold the key to preventing excessive \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  appreciation in Latin America."\par \par \uc2 Colombia has seen record foreign investment flow into the nation as security improvements lower the risk of exploring for oil, gold and other natural resources.\par \par \uc2 The flood of money, coupled with attractive yields compared with near-zero interest rates in developed nations, has bolstered the value of the peso.\par \par \uc2 Colombia's dollar purchase program previously ran through September 2011. The bank introduced a dollar option policy in October, but scrapped the program on Monday.\par \par \uc2 Policy makers last week raised the benchmark lending rate a quarter point to 5 percent to slow inflation and cool bank lending, bringing complaints from exporters of flowers and bananas that the move would attract additional capital, boost the peso and damage their business.\par \par \uc2 Luis Carlos Villegas, head of Colombia's main business group, known as Andi, said last week the bank had been "overly prudent" in raising the rate.\par \par \uc2 Exporters like flower growers have suffered from the strengthening peso because they pay costs in pesos and receive dollars for their sales. As many as 20,000 flower jobs have been lost in the last four years, most blamed on the strong \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In a bid to stem the peso's rise, the government said it would not bring in dollars for financing in 2012 and would keep $1 billion in dividends from state oil company \uc2 Ecopetrol\uc2 , and another $1.2 billion in royalties, abroad.\par \par \uc2 "We are surprised with how strong a hand the government has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market this year and wonder if it isn't becoming over concerned with the impact of rising interest rates on peso's relative performance given the disparity with the rest of the region and emerging markets in general," RBS said in a note.\par \par \uc2 Colombia's vote to increase the lending rate bucked the trend of other Latin American central banks that have either cut rates and kept them steady to shield their economies from the debt crisis in Europe and a global slowdown.\par \par \uc2 The government has said it would avoid imposing capital controls to prevent pressure on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and instead aim for long-term measures and micro-structural reforms. In 2007, it established unpopular capital controls - lifted later - to deter the entry of speculative money.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Helen Murphy Editing by W Simon)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-COLOMBIA/PESO (CORRECTED)   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020120206e8260019v\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
