\par\par \b \uc2 Colombia flower, banana growers clamor for peso measures\b0\par\par\uc2 564 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Februar 2012\par 20:33\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has firmed 6.2 pct so far in 2012\par \par \uc2 * Cenbank hiked key interest rate on Monday\par \par \uc2 * Sectors worry over speculative capital inflows\par \par \uc2 By Jack Kimball\par \par \uc2 BOGOTA, Feb 1 (Reuters) - Colombia's flower and banana industries pleaded with the government and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday to reign in the strengthening peso \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  after the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  hiked interest rates.\par \par \uc2 Colombia like other emerging markets is trying to tame inflation - the scourge of central banks worldwide - amid worries the Eurozone debt crisis and anemic U.S. growth might impact the local economy.\par \par \uc2 The Andean nation has bucked the trend in Latin America by hiking interest rates, the latest rate rise on Monday -- a move that curbs inflation but also puts upward pressure on the peso by making local assets more attractive.\par \par \uc2 Banana and flower exporters are among the biggest employers of rural Colombians and lead a lobby of exporters that have been the most vocal seeking a weaker \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "The rate hike (on Monday) is an invitation for speculative capital to come to the country in higher volumes, sharpening the revaluation process," the flower and banana growers industries said in a joint statement.\par \par \uc2 "Most worrying is that the measure to hike the interest rate has not even come accompanied by some exchange rate \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  given the space that exists to increase reserves."\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Colombia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's peso has firmed more than 6 percent so far this year, making the local unit one of the best performers of the world's 36 most-traded \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , partly thanks to strong foreign direct investment inflows.\par \par \uc2 The complaints from the flower and banana industries will add more pressure on policy makers to fight peso appreciation. However, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been less willing in the recent past to take major steps such as capital controls and preferred structural changes and dollar purchases.\par \par \uc2 Strengthening \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  hit exporters the most since they pay costs in local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  but receive dollars for their sales. Strong exchange rates can also help ease consumer prices by making imported goods cheaper.\par \par \uc2 In a move to stem the peso's rise, the government announced on Monday it would not bring in dollars for financing in 2012 and would keep $1 billion in \uc2 Ecopetrol\uc2  dividends and another $1.2 billion in royalties abroad.\par \par \uc2 Billions of dollars in foreign direct investment, mainly in the oil and mining sectors, have flowed into the country since a 2002 U.S.-backed offensive pushed leftist guerrillas back to ever-remoter jungle and mountain hideouts.\par \par \uc2 Once seen as a failing state, Colombia has begun to turn its image around by improving security, reigning in stubborn fiscal deficits and recouping three investment grade credit ratings from Wall Street that were lost in a 1999 financial crisis.\par \par \uc2 While interest rates remain low in developed economies, Colombia's relatively high rates create attractive differentials for investors and could bring in more dollars and drive more appreciation of its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 On Wednesday, the peso \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  firmed 0.85 percent to 1,794.85 versus the U.S. dollar - its highest level since September last year.\par \par \uc2 Since the start of the year, the peso has trended stronger, breaking through the 200-day moving average on a firming path after weakening to below that average from mid-September.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting By Jack Kimball; Editing by Andrew Hay)\par \par \uc2 COLOMBIA-\b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCY\b0 \highlight\uc2 /   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020120201e8210013m\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw427\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal6405\pichgoal600
