\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Colombia Central Bank Forex \highlight\uc2 - \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Free For Second Month\b0\par\par\uc2 239 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Dezember 2011\par 17:41\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 BOGOTA (Dow Jones)--\b \highlight22\uc2 Colombia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which bought an average of $411 million a month in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market during each of the first nine months of 2011 to limit peso strength, didn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  at all in October or November, it said Monday.\par \par \uc2 The bank's $3.72 billion in dollar purchases from January through September were part of a program that began last year to drain U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the market and stem peso strength that was due to a weak U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and heavy foreign investment that's seen dollars pour into Colombia.\par \par \uc2 But the bank allowed the program to expire at the end of September, as a global financial crisis caused investors to dump the peso and other Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which reversed their trend toward strength. Colombia's peso is 8% weaker since the beginning of September and was trading Monday at COP1,933 for a dollar.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in October implemented a new \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  volatility-prevention program in which it will buy or sell $200 million through put or call options on any day in which the peso's exchange rate moves 4% up or down from the 20-day moving average. But so far those boundaries haven't been touched.\par \par \uc2 -By Dan Molinski, Dow Jones Newswires; 57-310-867-6542; dan.molinski@dowjones.com [ 12-12-11 1641GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020111212e7cc000yi\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
