\par\par \b \uc2 DJ Colombia's Peso Extends Gains For 9th Straight Session\b0\par\par\uc2 408 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 April 2011\par 21:54\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2011, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 BOGOTA (Dow Jones)--The Colombian peso nudged a slight gain against the peso Monday, extending a trend that has seen the Colombian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strengthen against the dollar in recent days.\par \par \uc2 The peso closed at COP1,817 to the dollar from COP1,817.75 Friday, according to \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  data. It was the 9th straight session that the peso strengthened against the dollar, a tendency that could continue in the coming days.\par \par \uc2 Alianza Valores, a Bogota-based brokerage firm, said in a research note Monday that the exchange rate could dip below the COP1,800 level in the first half of the year.\par \par \uc2 A surge in exports in February, when they increased 37% from a year ago to reach $3.9 billion, is set to carry on thanks to high prices for oil and coal, Colombia's top exports. That is likely to continue fueling Colombia's economy but will also represent a strong exchange rate, said RBS Securities in a research note.\par \par \uc2 Colombia had been dogged by a strong peso, with exporters and trade unions in the past ramping up pressure on the government when the exchange rate nears the COP1,750 mark. The peso's strength has been fueled in large part by foreign investment into Colombia's commodities-rich economy.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the government, however, have avoided placing controls on foreign investment to curb the peso's strength. Instead, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has resorted to buying dollars in the spot market to the tune of $20 million daily to mop up U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , a move which also allows the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  to build up its international reserves. "\b \highlight22\uc2 Colombia\b0 \highlight\uc2  should continue to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market in an opportunistic way," RBS said in a research note.\par \par \uc2 Adding to the inflows of foreign investment, other factors are also pressuring the exchange rate. Colombia's foreign debt was raised to investment-grade last month by \uc2 Standard & Poor's\uc2  rating agency, opening the door for the institutional investors that have restrictions on investing in anything but investment-grade instruments.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also began raising interest rates in February, a move that could generate more portfolio investments into Colombia and lead to a stronger peso against the dollar.\par \par \uc2 -By Darcy Crowe, Dow Jones Newswires; (57) 1 703 8953; darcy.crowe@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 April 11, 2011 15:54 ET (19:54 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020110411e74b0050b\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw427\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal6405\pichgoal600
