\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK: Nomura Sees  \highlight22\uc2 Colombia FX Intervention \highlight\uc2  Ending\b0\par\par\uc2 140 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Februar 2011\par 18:03\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 12:03 (Dow Jones) \b \highlight22\uc2 Colombia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program that buys $20M each day expires on March 15, and strategists at Normua expect authorities not to renew it. Nomura forecasts a stronger peso down the line, with USD/COP reaching 1760 by year-end. Recent weakness in the Colombian peso can be attributed to the continued US dollar purchases being made by the nation's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , coupled with the fact that regulations prevent local \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  intermediaries from having direct short USD/COP positions, they said. The dollar was recently at COP1887.7, up from COP1841.2 on Jan. 21. (cynthia.lin@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 Call us at (212) 416-2354 or email kevin.kingsbury@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 Visit the Market Talk blog at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.djnmarkettalk.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.djnmarkettalk.com}}}\uc2  [ 09-02-11 1703GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1012 1085   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110209e729001ji\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
