\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Colombia cenbank says bought $400 mln in Oct\b0\par\par\uc2 127 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 November 2010\par 21:34\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  (Adds context)\par \par \uc2  BOGOTA, Nov 8 (Reuters) - Colombia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Monday that it bought $400 million in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in October as part of its effort to control the strength of the peso <COP=RR>.\par \par \uc2  The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has strengthened 8.27 percent over the last 12 months to 1,817.7 per U.S. dollar.\par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has bought $2.24 billion so far this year as local exporters clamor for a weaker peso.\par \par \uc2  On Friday, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief Jose Dario Uribe said policymakers will consider "big \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 " as part of the effort.  (Reporting by Javier Mozzo)  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 COLOMBIA\b0 \highlight\uc2 -\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTIONS\b0 \highlight\uc2 / (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|E|RBN|D|M|RNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020101108e6b8001om\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
