\par\par \b \uc2 Colombia talks peso, markets eye capital controls\b0\par\par\uc2 637 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Oktober 2010\par 21:04\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Peso down 3.4 pct in two weeks on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  fears\par \par \uc2 * Santos talks about IMF and capital controls in speech\par \par \uc2 By Jack Kimball and Nelson Bocanegra\par \par \uc2 BOGOTA, Oct 27 (Reuters) - Comments by the Colombian government indicate higher chances it will use short-term capital controls to temper the country's rising peso, Colombian analysts said on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Colombian President Juan Manuel Santos on Wednesday said he was surprised the International Monetary Fund now saw capital controls as a way to curb sudden surges in money flowing into emerging markets.\par \par \uc2 "I didn't think I'd live to see a head of the IMF saying that suddenly there are some capital controls that should be imposed. That for me is a total paradigm shift but it's the reality," Santos said in a speech.\par \par \uc2 Economic observers say some companies are speculating in the Andean nation, taking advantage of cheap money in developed markets and making carry trades in Colombia -- a reason why the market expects some short-term capital controls.\par \par \uc2 While the government has said it would take new measures against the peso this week, Bogota has not said what the move might be and is weighing a number of options. Analysts say the signs indicate some form of short-term capital controls.\par \par \uc2 "This is simply anticipating information that could come on Friday on the side of capital controls on external debt," said Camilo Perez, head of economic research at \uc2 Banco de Bogota\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 A Reuters poll of analysts found the majority think the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will announce additional \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  measures at its meeting on Friday, with the most probable move seen as a control on short-term capital inflows. [ID:nN25272647] <^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\par \par \uc2 For a graphic on Colombia's battle with its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 :\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://r.reuters.com/muq52q"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://r.reuters.com/muq52q}}}\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Colombia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2           [ID:nN24243857]\par  Scenarios on possible peso moves       [ID:nN15183902]\par  Global money flows and strategy        [ID:nINVEST]\par   ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^>\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 While a recent G20 meeting pledged to move towards market-determined exchange rates and called for measures to reduce excessive external imbalances, investors saw no reason to change their view of stronger emerging \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . [ID:nTOE69K01G]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Many emerging economies are concerned that the rush of speculative inflows in recent months could create potentially destabilizing bubbles, making policymaking more difficult.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In Latin America, high commodity prices and strong growth have attracted a slew of investors. Nations in the region, such as Brazil and Peru, have moved to curb their \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 At the weekend, Santos said the government would announce measures this week to help mitigate the impact of the rising peso \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  <COP=RR>. [ID:nN23159856]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has restarted a dollar buying program to try to stop the rise of the peso, which has surged 11 percent this year. The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , however, has eased 3.49 percent in the last two weeks on fears of more \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Colombia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's markets are enjoying strong demand thanks to growing expectations it may soon regain an investment-grade rating -- net foreign portfolio inflows were $179 million, with $951 million flowing in and $772 million flowing out.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 From January to September, net foreign loans of the private sector were negative $80 million, with $5.97 billion entering the nation and $6.05 billion leaving as debt repayments, according to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  data.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The answer isn't easy because capital movements toward the developing world are being produced globally. That's why it's necessary to have a battery of instruments," former finance minister, Jose Antonio Ocampo, wrote in a local paper.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Without a competitive exchange rate, investment exports different from mining and hydrocarbons will not take place and some companies will go out of business," Ocampo wrote. (Editing by Frank Jack Daniel; Editing by Andrew Hay)\f28 \par \par \uc2 COLOMBIA-\b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCY\b0 \highlight\uc2 /|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|D|E|RBN|RNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020101027e6ar001qx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
