\par\par \b \uc2 PREVIEW-Colombia cenbank rate seen stable, eyes on peso\b0\par\par\uc2 430 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Oktober 2010\par 20:55\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 WHAT: Colombia's monthly \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy meeting\par \par \uc2 WHEN: Friday, Oct. 29\par \par \uc2 OUTCOME: Bank seen keeping benchmark rate at 3 percent\par \par \uc2 REUTERS FORECAST:\par \par \uc2 A Reuters poll of 40 analysts found that nearly all observers expected the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to leave its key interest rate at 3 percent at its monthly meeting on Friday. Only two analysts saw a reduction in the rate.\par \par \uc2 Of the observers surveyed, 27 said that they expected the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  to announce additional measures against the surging peso \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , with the most probable move seen as a control on capital inflows from external debt.\par \par \uc2 Looking longer term, nearly all of those polled estimated the bank would keep its benchmark interest rate stable until year end, and more than two-thirds think that the rate will close 2011 between 4 percent and 4.5 percent.\par \par \uc2 FACTORS TO WATCH:\par \par \uc2 With the interest rate likely to remain unchanged, all eyes will be on the bank's remarks on the peso and possible measures the board could announce to slow the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rise. For more details on possible measures, click [ID:nN15183902]\par \par \uc2 In mid-September, the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  restarted a dollar purchasing program of at least $20 million daily. President Juan Manuel Santos said on Saturday that the government would announce measures this week to help mitigate the impact of the rising peso \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  <COP=RR>. [ID:nN23159856]\par \par \uc2 The government and the bank have been under pressure to do more to control the strengthening \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Other nations in the region, such as Brazil and Peru, have also moved to curb their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . For a Factbox on \b \highlight22\uc2 Colombia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's past \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , click [ID:nN24243857]\par \par \uc2 "Concerning \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  measures, we don't rule out capital controls, especially for private external debt," said consultants EConcept in a note.\par \par \uc2 "However, to the extent that international conditions and daily \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  are able to keep the exchange rate above 1,800 pesos per dollar, the probability of placing those controls is reduced."\par \par \uc2 MARKET IMPACT:\par \par \uc2 Maintaining the interest rate is unlikely to move the peso or local peso-denominated TES bonds as the market will have factored that into its trading options.\par \par \uc2 But there is a lot of interest in peso measures although many players have already adjusted their positions to account for likely moves by the government or \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . (Reporting by Nelson Bocanegra; Writing by Jack Kimball; Editing by Frank Jack Daniel and Diane Craft)\par \par \uc2 COLOMBIA-RATES/ (PREVIEW)|LANGEN|Table|ABN|E|RBN|M|D|U|RNP|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020101025e6ap001lr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
