\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-Colombia eyes peso measures, firming trend remains\b0\par\par\uc2 679 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Oktober 2010\par 17:03\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Santos gives no details of possible actions to curb peso\par \par \uc2 * Peso has gained 12 percent year-to-date against dollar\par \par \uc2 * Colombia can't avoid the change in dollar's value - IMF (Recasts, adds analyst, details)\par \par \uc2 By Jack Kimball and Javier Mozzo\par \par \uc2 BOGOTA, Oct 19 (Reuters) - Colombia's government vowed to act to tackle the economic impact of the country's strong peso and the International Monetary Fund said on Tuesday the Andean nation could not avoid the change in the dollar's value.\par \par \uc2 Latin America's No. 4 oil producer has seen its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strengthen due to inflows into its mining and energy sectors, dollar sales to finance government spending and a recovery from the global financial crisis.\par \par \uc2 The peso <COP=RR> has surged around 12 percent against the dollar so far this year to the chagrin of battered exporters who receive earnings in dollars but pay costs in pesos.\par \par \uc2 "We have to look out so that our economy is not affected by a stronger revaluation from which the rest of the world is (also) suffering," President Juan Manuel Santos told La Republica newspaper. "We're going to take action."\par \par \uc2 "Very soon we'll announce a package of measures to face this phenomenon in addition to what the government and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  have already done," he was quoted as saying.\par \par \uc2 Santos gave no details on possible measures.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  announced in mid-September a dollar purchasing program of at least $20 million a day to try to contain the rising peso. For more see [ID:nN15145483].\par \par \uc2 In Latin America, high commodity prices and strong growth have attracted a slew of investors, increasing capital inflows that boost local \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Other nations in the region, such as Brazil and Peru, have moved to curb their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . <^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Colombia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  past market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2      [ID:nN24243857]\par  Steps other countries are taking       [ID:nSGE69503F]\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^>\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 GOOD NEWS, BAD NEWS\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Santos reiterated government plans to cut the costs of doing business. Bogota presented a reform bill to Congress last week including a cut in the energy surtax. [ID:nN15219226]\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Colombia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 monetary authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  also modified its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rules last week to make it easier for the bank to enter the market. [ID:nN15189451]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The government has said it would receive two dividend payments abroad from state-controlled \f28 \uc2 \f2 Ecopetrol\f28 \uc2 \f2  oil company worth about $1.4 billion. [ID:nN13283686]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The measures adopted by the authorities so far may signal that policymakers are trying to avoid more onerous administrative controls ... that's the good news," Daniel Volberg of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Morgan Stanley\f28 \uc2 \f2  said in a recent note.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The bad news is that none of the measures the authorities have adopted so far appear to have broken the peso's advance," he said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The world's No. 5 coal exporter has seen a boom in oil and mining investment since the government in 2002 launched a U.S.-backed offensive against leftist rebels which opened up areas of the country once under guerrillas control.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Colombia's largest coal exporter, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Cerrejon\f28 \uc2 \f2 , said on Monday that its costs have been raised by the effect of the strong domestic \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  against the U.S. dollar. [ID:nLDE69H1EZ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Colombian firms and exporters have called on the government to take more measures against the rising \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  such as accumulating more international reserves. [ID:nN11111019]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Nicolas Eyzaguirre, head of the International Monetary Fund's Western Hemisphere Department, said it would be impossible for Colombia to avoid a stronger peso \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  due to strong growth and investment in mining.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Colombia finds itself in an auspicious phase, not cyclical but structural for the development of its mining sector and there are fundamental and structural factors that make this economy attractive for foreign investment," Eyzaguirre told journalists in Colombia's capital, Bogota.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "And it follows that the value of the dollar will be more moderate than what it was in recent years and trying to avoid that reality is not going to be possible." (Editing by James Dalgleish)\f28 \par \par \uc2 COLOMBIA-\b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCY\b0 \highlight\uc2 / (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|D   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020101019e6aj00162\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
