\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1- \highlight22\uc2 Colombia \highlight\uc2  cenbank modifies  \highlight22\uc2 forex intervention \highlight\uc2  rules\b0\par\par\uc2 385 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Oktober 2010\par 16:25\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Peso falls on \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's announcement\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Colombia\b0 \highlight\uc2  cenbank under pressure to do more against peso (Adds background, peso details)\par \par \uc2 BOGOTA, Oct 15 (Reuters) - Colombia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it had modified its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rules to make it easier for the bank to enter the market discretionally and help control the surging local peso \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Colombia's peso -- which has been strengthening this year -- closed down 0.43 percent to 1,809.10 against the dollar, with investors seeing the modifications as an indication the bank could step up \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Last month, the bank started buying at least $20 million daily through auctions to help stem the rise of the peso, which has firmed more than 10 percent so far this year. The private sector has called for the government to do more.\par \par \uc2 The new rules, issued late on Thursday, made it easier for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market at its own discretion as it can now participate in a private-initiative clearing house created for \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  transactions in 2008.\par \par \uc2 The bank stopped \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  discretionally in the market in 2007, according to traders.\par \par \uc2 For a copy of the changes in Spanish, click {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.banrep.gov.co/documentos/reglamentacion/cambiaria/2010/29.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.banrep.gov.co/documentos/reglamentacion/cambiaria/2010/29.pdf}}}\par \par \uc2 Colombia's rule change follows moves by other emerging country governments that have sought to stem the rise of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , stop their economies overheating and defend exporters. Authorities in Brazil and Peru have tried to curb their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Colombia's announcement offset expected gains by the peso after Fitch Ratings revised its outlook on Colombia's sovereign credit to positive from stable -- the third major ratings agency to upgrade its outlook this year. [ID:nN14147465]\par \par \uc2 On Thursday, \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Jose Dario Uribe said foreign capital of the private sector had been net negative this year, and more debt payments by Colombians were flowing out than loans coming in. [ID:nN14129204]\par \par \uc2 Analysts said the governor's comments suggested he thought it may not make sense to use capital controls, but observers said the bank's board was also split over the issue.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Nelson Bocanegra and Jack Kimball; Editing by Andrew Hay)\par \par \uc2 COLOMBIA-\b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCY\b0 \highlight\uc2 / (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|E|RBN|M|D|U|RNP|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020101015e6af0014v\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
