\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Colombia's peso down on cenbank, region weak\b0\par\par\uc2 530 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Oktober 2010\par 16:18\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Dollar's recovery curbs regional rally\par \par \uc2 * Colombia's peso falls on \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rule change\par \par \uc2 * Chilean peso flat after rates raised slightly\par \par \uc2 (Adds comments, updates prices)\par \par \uc2 By Caroline Stauffer and Samantha Pearson\par \par \uc2 MEXICO CITY/SAO PAULO, Oct 15 (Reuters) - Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakened on Friday as investors bet the dollar's recent decline was overdone and Colombia's peso fell after new rules cleared the way for more \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Bets the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will soak up safe-haven debt and drive down borrowing costs in the United States, a policy tool known as quantitative easing, have lifted demand for higher yielding assets like Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 But U.S. Federal Reserve Chairman Ben Bernanke said on Friday policymakers were still weighing how aggressive they should be. [ID:nLDE69E1EV]\par \par \uc2 After sinking to multi-month lows against a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Fed expectations, the dollar recovered. The Brazilian real and the Mexican peso weakened as a result.\par \par \uc2 "The Euro's decline against the dollar indicated the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market had already priced in a lot of quantitative easing potential - that's why Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are adjusting to the weak side today," Robert Melzi, a strategist at \uc2 Barclays Capital\uc2  in New York said.\par \par \uc2 Mexico's peso <MXN=>shed 0.21 percent to 12.4125 while Brazil's real <BRBY> slipped 0.18 percent to 1.664.\par \par \uc2 Brazil's Finance Minister Guido Mantega told reporters on Friday the government was waiting for \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to stabilize before taking fresh measures to curb the real's rise. [ID:nN15201659]\par \par \uc2 The threat of more aggressive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 Colombia\b0 \highlight\uc2 , however, prompted the country's peso to close 0.43 percent weaker to 1800.10 per dollar.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  issued new rules late on Thursday, making it easier for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market at its own discretion. [ID:nN15204150]\par \par \uc2 The Chilean peso <CLP=> closed flat at 478.8 per dollar, the day after the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  raised the country's benchmark interest rate by 25 basis points to 2.75 percent.\par \par \uc2 The bank has slowed the pace at which it raises rates for fear that higher rates would fuel an even bigger rally in the peso, which is trading around a 29-month high.\par \par \uc2 But the threats kept coming. Chile's peso appreciation is worrying and could soon have an adverse effect on economic activity and inflation, \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  board member Enrique Marshall said in a presentation posted on the bank's website on Friday. [ID:nN15190638]\par \par \uc2 Mexico's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Friday held its target for overnight bank lending at 4.5 percent, the lowest since policymakers began targeting the rate in January 2008.\par \par \uc2 Mexico has maintained record-low interest rates as foreign investors looking for bigger returns pour cash into Latin America.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said that "these capital inflows have contributed to the recent appreciation of the exchange rate, the accumulation of international reserves and continues reducing interest rates along the yield curve." [ID:nN15196452]\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-LATAM/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|ABN|E|RBN|D|M|RNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020101018e6af0012i\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
