\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Colombia cenbank chief talks peso, capital flows\b0\par\par\uc2 735 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Oktober 2010\par 18:02\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  * Colombia battles strengthening peso \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  * Analysts: cenbank board of two minds on capital controls\par \par \uc2  * Fiscal issues could limit dollar purchases-analysts  (Adds fiscal details, analyst)\par \par \uc2  By Nelson Bocanegra and Jack Kimball\par \par \uc2  BOGOTA, Oct 14 (Reuters) - Colombian \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Jose Dario Uribe said on Thursday foreign capital of the private sector had been net negative this year and more debt payments by Colombians were flowing out than loans coming in.\par \par \uc2  The Andean nation's monetary body is under pressure by Colombian firms to do more to combat the rising peso \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but the governor's comments suggest he thinks it may not make sense now to use capital controls, analysts said.\par \par \uc2  "We've said that from our viewpoint, we have instruments that we use to the extent and intensity that we consider appropriate ... there are other instruments that so far we have not employed because we consider that the costs outweigh the benefits," Uribe told local Radio W.\par \par \uc2  "External capital of the private sector, distinct from foreign direct investment, is still net negative. That means despite a growth in disbursements of foreign credit, Colombians are paying more credit in even larger amounts outward and hence what they pay outward surpasses what is entering from abroad.\par \par \uc2  "So that's still not a factor that's weighing on what's happening with the exchange rate," he said. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par   <^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Colombia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2           [ID:nN24243857]\par  Latin American interest rates          [ID:nN08199099]\par  Comments by policymakers on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  [ID:nSGE695036]\par  Global \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  war report: \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://r.reuters.com/dyw27p"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://r.reuters.com/dyw27p}}}\uc2 \f2 \par   ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^>\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  In mid-September, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  announced a dollar\par purchasing program of at least $20 million daily for a minimum\par of four months to try to ease the strengthening peso, which has\par risen more than 10 percent versus the dollar so far this year.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  From January to September, net foreign loans of the private\par sector were negative $80 million, with $5.97 billion entering\par the nation and $6.05 billion leaving as debt repayments,\par according to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  data.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  While Colombia's markets are enjoying strong demand thanks\par to growing expectations it may soon regain an investment-grade\par rating, net foreign portfolio inflows were $179 million, with\par $951 million flowing in and $772 million flowing out.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  Despite calls for more \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , neither the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  nor the finance ministry has taken any new measures since\par the Sept. 15 dollar buying program. [ID:nN15145483]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  "That reflects that there are two positions on capital\par controls inside the (\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's) board," said Camilo Perez,\par head of economic research at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Banco de Bogota\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  FISCAL CONCERNS\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  Latin America's No. 4 oil producer has seen a five-fold\par increase in foreign direct investment, mainly in oil and\par mining, since a 2002 U.S.-backed security crackdown on leftist\par rebels.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  The World Bank said Latin America should moderate fiscal\par spending to help central banks tame rapidly appreciating\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . Authorities in Brazil and Peru have moved to curb\par their \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . [ID:nN24260311]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  Finance Minister Juan Carlos Echeverry said late on\par Wednesday the government would ask lawmakers to eliminate a tax\par deduction for investment beginning next year. [ID:nN13286688]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  The tax deduction -- which is currently 30 percent -- would\par save the nation 0.8 percent of gross domestic product,\par according to the government. The peso <COP=RR> fell 0.73\par percent on Thursday to 1,804 pesos against the greenback from\par Wednesday's close after the finance minister's statement.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  Analysts say the amount of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's dollar buys\par could be limited by fiscal issues since the government must\par take on the bank's operating losses. Tackling the deficit is\par one of the main challenges for the government, especially as it\par seeks to recover investment grade lost during the 1990s.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  For a graphic on Colombia's credit rating, click on:\par \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/tav35n"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/tav35n}}}\par \par \uc2 \f2  "In general terms, a more accelerated accumulation of\par international reserves would mean very likely a growth in\par financial losses by the bank," economic expert Cesar Gonzalez\par wrote in a column in the financial newspaper Portafolio.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  "The finance minister will have to put that money on the\par table no later than April next year ... those asking the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to accumulate lower-yielding international assets,\par must take into account the fiscal costs."\par  (Additional reporting by Javier Mozzo; Editing by Dan\par Grebler)\par \par \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 COLOMBIA-\b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCY\b0 \highlight\uc2 / (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|Table|ABN|E|RBN|D|M|RNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020101014e6ae001cm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
