\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Latam  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\uc2  mixed on  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  fears\b0\par\par\uc2 586 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Oktober 2010\par 16:59\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Brazil's real drops 0.42 pct, Mexican peso down 0.03\par \par \uc2 * Colombia's peso closes at highest since August 2008\par \par \uc2 * Chile's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  president warns of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 (Updates prices, adds details on \b \highlight22\uc2 Colombia\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Chile)\par \par \uc2 By Samantha Pearson and Caroline Stauffer\par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO/MEXICO CITY (Reuters) - Brazil's real weakened sharply Wednesday after the government authorized its treasury to increase its dollar purchases on the local market as the country steps up efforts to halt appreciation.\par \par \uc2 The real was bid 0.42 percent weaker at 1.680 per U.S. dollar on the local spot market.\par \par \uc2 "The government is going to make an effort to adopt more measures to get control of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in this \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  war that is going on worldwide," said Luiz Eduardo Portella, a fixed-income and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader at Brazil's Banco Modal.\par \par \uc2 Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  announced Wednesday it had extended to 1,500 days its maximum period for contracts to be settled in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.\par \par \uc2 That would allow the treasury to buy more dollars. But confusion over the move prompted speculation that a much bigger measure was in the works, causing the real to plunge.\par \par \uc2 Brazil has stepped up its efforts to contain the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's appreciation recently, Tuesday raising a tax on bond purchases by foreigners. The tax did little to tame the real's recent rally.\par \par \uc2 "To me the Brazilians have signaled another step up the ladder," said Win Thin, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 Brown Brothers Harriman\uc2  in New York. "I think they may adjust the tax again."\par \par \uc2 Chile's peso strengthened 0.11 percent to 482.25 per dollar as the price of copper, the country's main export, extended its rally. The peso has rallied nearly 13 percent since the end of July.\par \par \uc2 Chile's \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President Jose De Gregorio said Wednesday the bank could \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to halt a sharp appreciation of the peso.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Colombia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's peso also gained 0.69 percent to close at 1789.05, its highest level in more than two years.\par \par \uc2 In mid-September, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  started purchasing what it said would be at least $20 million daily for at least four months to help ease the peso's rise and investors fear additional measures will be taken.\par \par \uc2 "There's some investor caution because these are the levels that make the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  uncomfortable," said Gustavo Sorzano, an analyst at Helm Bank in Bogota.\par \par \uc2 EYEING THE FED\par \par \uc2 Markets have been factoring in the prospect of the U.S. Federal Reserve announcing new asset purchase plans since the Bank of Japan eased monetary policy on Tuesday. A broadly weaker dollar has boosted emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 An unexpected fall in U.S. private sector employment on Wednesday led analysts to believe U.S. non-farm payroll reports due Friday could disappoint, which would further pressure the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to try to stimulate the economy.\par \par \uc2 Mexico's peso edged down 0.028 percent to 12.477 per dollar in volatile trading.\par \par \uc2 "The prospect of Fed easing is generally good for riskier assets, but if the Fed is considering quantitative easing, it shows they are really worried about economic recovery - that's the other side of the coin for Mexico," said \uc2 Brown Brothers Harriman\uc2 's Thin.\par \par \uc2 (Additional reporting by Maria Jose Latorre and Brad Haynes in Santiago, Nelson Bocanegra in Bogota and Silvio Cascione in Sao Paulo; Editing by Andrew Hay)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-LATAM/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 3)|LANGEN|FUN   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020101009e6a6000fq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
