\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Brazil real up on inflows,Colombia peso eases\b0\par\par\uc2 608 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 September 2010\par 22:33\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Repeats to additional subscribers)\par \par \uc2 * Brazil's real up 0.12 pct, Mexican peso down 0.1 pct\par \par \uc2 * Colombia peso loses steam ahead of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  meeting\par \par \uc2 * Copper rally boosts Chilean peso to 2-year closing high (Adds commentary, updates prices)\par \par \uc2 By Caroline Stauffer and Samantha Pearson\par \par \uc2 MEXICO CITY/SAO PAULO, Sept 23 (Reuters) - Brazil's real strengthened on Thursday as capital poured into Brazil ahead of a huge stock offering, while Colombia's peso weakened ahead of a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  meeting.\par \par \uc2 The real <BRBY> bid 0.12 percent stronger at 1.717 reais per U.S. dollar on the local spot market as investors prepared for a $79 billion offering by state-controlled oil company \uc2 Petrobras\uc2  that is expected to price later on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 But trading was very volatile. Although huge amounts of dollars are expected to enter Brazil's market over the next couple of days, traders were worried about recent threats by the government to use the sovereign wealth fund to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "Investors are still weighing up the power of the sovereign wealth fund in the short-term," said Cristiano Oliveira, chief economist for Banco Safra de Investimento in Sao Paulo. "There is a battle to contain the real's appreciation and now this other player has turned up and it's one that is heavily armed."\par \par \uc2 Brazil's government on Monday authorized the use of its sovereign wealth fund to buy U.S. dollars in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market as part of efforts to weaken the real. [ID:nN20102448] The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  already \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market on a daily basis, buying dollars.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the rising price of copper, Chile's main export, helped to boost the country's peso to a 2-year closing high against the dollar.\par \par \uc2 The peso <CLP=> firmed 0.9 percent to 488.50 per dollar, closing at its strongest level since June 2008.\par \par \uc2 "The only fundamental favoring the peso right now is the rebounding price of copper," said one trader in Santiago.\par \par \uc2 The peso has appreciated more than 10 percent since early July, prompting \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  warnings from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which analysts expect to step in if the peso firms past 480 per dollar. [ID:nN19249922]\par \par \uc2 COLOMBIAN PESO LAGS\par \par \uc2 Colombia's peso <COP=RR> shed 0.35 percent to 1811.25 on fears the country could take further measures to curb its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rally.\par \par \uc2 "Colombia's peso has been a regional star, and today it is losing a little bit of steam," Nomura Economist Benito Berber said. "My suspicion is that it might have to do with the likely announcement of additional \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  policies."\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Colombia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  meets on Friday and some economists believe further \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  measures could be announced.\par \par \uc2 The peso has strengthened 11.77 percent this year, leading the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to begin purchasing dollars to help slow its ascent on Sept. 15.\par \par \uc2 Mexico's peso <MXN=> traded nearly even, shedding 0.08 percent to 12.6378 per dollar.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has gained nearly 5 percent in September, boosted in part by foreign investors buying Mexico's peso ahead of the country's inclusion in October in a major global bond index run by \uc2 Citigroup\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "The peso is a very good deal around 12.62 and we are seeing foreigners buying in," said Enrique Trejo, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading at brokerage IXE in Mexico City. (Additional reporting by Froilan Romera in Santiago, Nelson Bocanegra in Bogota and Jean Luis Arce in Mexico City; Editing by Dan Grebler)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-LATAM/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)(REPEAT)|LANGEN|ABN|D|E|RBN|M|U|RNP|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100926e69n000e0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw427\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal6405\pichgoal600
