\par\par \b \uc2 Colombia  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Buys $20 Mln On Spot Market At COP1,798\b0\par\par\uc2 137 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 September 2010\par 22:49\par \uc2 Dow Jones News Service\par \uc2 DJ\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 BOGOTA (Dow Jones)--\b \highlight22\uc2 Colombia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market Monday to purchase $20 million at 1,798 Colombian pesos per U.S. dollar.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  started purchasing dollars last Wednesday, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb the peso's appreciation and build up international reserves. The bank said it will buy at least $20 million a day for at least four months. Finance Minister Juan Carlos Echeverry Friday said the bank could buy much more than $20 million per day.\par \par \uc2 The Colombian peso has been appreciating about 13% so far this year.\par \par \uc2 On Monday, the peso ended unchanged at COP1,799.80 per dollar.\par \par \uc2 -By Inti Landauro, Dow Jones Newswires; 57-1-694 00 76, colombia@dowjones.com [ 09-20-10 1649ET ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJ00000020100920e69k000sq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
