\par\par \b \uc2 Colombia exporters call for added peso measures\b0\par\par\uc2 644 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 September 2010\par 19:38\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited    \par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  urged to lower key interest rate\par \par \uc2 * Coffee players hit by peso despite high bean prices\par \par \uc2 By Javier Mozzo and Diana Delgado\par \par \uc2 BOGOTA, Sept 16 (Reuters) - Colombian exporters said on Thursday the government should help lower the cost of doing business and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  should take more measures to help firms weather a strengthening peso \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Various Latin American economies have seen their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  contend with appreciation this year due to high rates of growth and foreign investment inflows.\par \par \uc2 Regional powerhouse Brazil is aggressively buying dollars, Peru is tightening deposit requirements and Chile has warned it may have to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Colombia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's peso -- one of the region's strongest-performing \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  -- has firmed around 12 percent this year, hurting exporter profits and prompting the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to restart dollar purchases. For details, see [ID:nN15145483]\par \par \uc2 Luis Carlos Villegas, president of the National Association of Colombian Entrepreneurs, said the bank should lower its benchmark interest rate -- currently 3 percent, down from 10 percent in 2008. He also said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had scope to increase its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves from the current eight months of import cover.\par \par \uc2 "You have to look at this in the medium and long term because what is needed is not that the (peso/dollar rate) go to 2,000 or 2,200 pesos, but that in the next five years the exchange rate remains at competitive levels," he told local radio.\par \par \uc2 The peso <COP=RR> fell 0.30 percent to 1,812.50 at 1300 EDT (1700 GMT) from Wednesday's close.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's monthly meeting will be held on Sept. 24 where analysts say the body could take more measures to combat the peso's rise and may even lower the key rate.\par \par \uc2 Trade Minister Sergio Diaz Granados told Reuters in a recent interview that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could have room to purchase up to $9 billion if the government's fiscal reforms were passed by lawmakers. [ID:nN15156198]\par \par \uc2 Colombia has seen a boom in foreign investment, particularly in the oil and mining industries, as its decades-long guerrilla conflict ebbs, adding appreciation pressures on the peso. The country is now Latin America's No. 4 oil producer and a major exporter of coal, coffee, flowers and nickel.\par \par \uc2 MORE ACTION\par \par \uc2 The coffee federation in Colombia, which is the world's top exporter of high-quality washed Arabica beans, says the peso's rise cost the sector as much as 55 billion pesos ($30.5 million) in the first half of 2010.\par \par \uc2 "The appreciation has harmed us a lot. High international coffee prices aren't benefiting us much because buyers at some point sought coffee in other parts of the world where the premium for coffee is not as high as Colombia," said Juan Arboleda, a coffee exporter in the Antioquia province,\par \par \uc2 Analysts said the central's bank's dollar purchases would help in the short term, but could not rule out the bank and the government taking more aggressive steps later in the year. For scenarios on possible measures, double-click on [ID:nN15183902]\par \par \uc2 The government of President Juan Manuel Santos is trying to push a raft of reforms through Colombia's legislature -- including new fiscal rules -- which it hopes will help the country get back the coveted investment-grade ratings status.\par \par \uc2 Javier Diaz, president of the National Association of External Trade, said that the government needed to help companies lower borrowing costs as well as costs for transport and electricity to help the firms be more competitive.\par \par \uc2 "Complementary actions are needed because (accumulating reserves) by itself does not guarantee that the dollar is going to maintain a rising tendency," he said. "We need to see how to obtain lower costs for the productive machine."\par \par \uc2 COLOMBIA-\b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCY\b0 \highlight\uc2 /EXPORTERS|LANGEN|ABN|E|RBN|D|M|RNP    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100916e69g001dn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
