\par\par \b \uc2 INTERVIEW-Colombia sees difficult recovery for Venezuela trade\b0\par\par\uc2 583 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 September 2010\par 18:51\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Colombia exporters owed $800 mln in debts from Venezuela\par \par \uc2 * Room for \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy $7 bln-$9 bln in reserves\par \par \uc2 By Javier Mozzo\par \par \uc2 BOGOTA, Sept 15 (Reuters) - Colombian trade with neighboring Venezuela will "never" return to its previous levels, Bogota's trade minister said, after a spat whittled billions-of-dollars-a-year in commerce down to a trickle.\par \par \uc2 Strained ties between Colombia, the U.S. top ally in Latin America, and Venezuela's socialist government have periodically ratcheted up tensions in the volatile Andean region.\par \par \uc2 Bilateral trade rose to $7 billion two years ago, but slid after Venezuelan leader Hugo Chavez partially froze commerce to protest a deal that gave Washington more access to Colombian military bases.\par \par \uc2 "Clearly commerce with Venezuela is never going to be what it was in the past," Sergio Diaz Granados, Colombia's Minister for Trade, Industry and Tourism, told Reuters in an interview.\par \par \uc2 "The Venezuela that we're going to work with in the coming years is very distinct from the one (Colombia) has worked with in the last 10 or 15 years," he said late on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 Relations have improved since Colombian President Juan Manuel Santos took office last month -- after the former government accused Caracas of harboring leftist Colombian rebels, prompting Chavez to briefly break off diplomatic ties.\par \par \uc2 Santos and Chavez have said they will set up a commission to look into restoring bilateral commercial ties.\par \par \uc2 Colombian exports to Venezuela are expected to plummet to $1 billion this year, Bogota says, well below last year's $4 billion and $6 billion in 2008. Exports averaged around $1 billion annually between 1995 and 2000.\par \par \uc2 Granados also said Venezuelan companies had paid $72 million of an estimated $800 million owed to Colombian exporters.\par \par \uc2 PESO AND \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 Separately, he said \b \highlight22\uc2 Colombia\b0 \highlight\uc2  expected to attract more than $10 billion in foreign direct investment this year.\par \par \uc2 After the government pushes through its fiscal plans, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would have room to purchase up to $9 billion and help contain the rising peso <COP=RR>, Granados said before the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  announced that it would restart dollar purchases.\par \par \uc2 Colombia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Wednesday it would begin purchasing at least $20 million daily for the next four months to help ease the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rise. For details, see [ID:nN15145483]\par \par \uc2 "There have been other initiatives (to manage the exchange rate) such as asking the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  for greater action once the government gets approval of its fiscal laws and it could ... ask the bank to make more effort," Granados said.\par \par \uc2 "Today the international reserves are at a maximum seven months of imports and eleven years ago they were eleven months, (so) there is room for the bank to buy at least between $7 billion and $9 billion," he said, without giving more details.\par \par \uc2 Since taking office in August, the Santos administration has proposed an ambitious set of reforms ranging from the management of oil and mining royalties, and agrarian land reform, to overhauling the health and justice systems.\par \par \uc2 Tackling a stubborn fiscal deficit is one of the main challenges for the government, especially as the country seeks to recover the investment grade rating it lost during a 1990s fiscal crisis. [ID:nN16265600] [ID:nN09190061]\par \par \uc2 "The condition (to announce the purchases of dollars) will be when the fiscal reforms are passed," Granados said.\par \par \uc2 COLOMBIA-TRADE/ (INTERVIEW)|LANGEN|ABN|E|RBN|D|M|C|GRO|MTL|SOF|O|OIL   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100918e69f000as\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
