\par\par \b \uc2 Colombian Peso Climbs As Authorities Mull  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 257 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 September 2010\par 00:04\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 BOGOTA (Dow Jones)--The \b \highlight22\uc2 Colombia\b0 \highlight\uc2  peso continued to gain on Tuesday against the dollar, reaching its strongest level in more than two years while authorities consider possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to rein in the peso.\par \par \uc2 The peso closed at COP1,790.35 to the dollar, stronger than COP1,791.3 on Monday. Finance Minister Juan Carlos Echeverry, speaking to reporters, blamed the peso's recent strength on a broader move away from the dollar in international markets.\par \par \uc2 The peso has gained more than 13%, and analysts have been anticipating a potential \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  since the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  breached COP1,800 to the dollar last week. "We're analyzing measures," Echeverry said, adding that "\b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is a measure that is available."\par \par \uc2 Asked if the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market before its monetary policy meeting slated for Sept. 24, Echeverry said it "very well may," but he didn't give any more details.\par \par \uc2 The IGBC benchmark stock index for Colombia climbed 0.46% to 14,193.31 points. The index was boosted by Pacific Rubiales Energy( PRE.T), which is also listed in Canada. The company announced Tuesday the successful exploration of a well in the Llanos Basin in Colombia. Pacific Rubiales rose 2.35% to COP44,420.\par \par \uc2 The yield on the benchmark 2020 bond stood at 7.300%, down from 7.385% Monday.\par \par \uc2 -By Darcy Crowe, Dow Jones Newswires; (57) 1 703 8953; darcy.crowe@dowjones.com [ 14-09-10 2204GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020100914e69e001aj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
