\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK: Colombian Peso Gains Heighten Capital Control Risk\b0\par\par\uc2 1,027 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 September 2010\par 20:55\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in New York.  Darlene Ross, 212 416-2166; \par darlene.ross@dowjones.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1853 GMT [Dow Jones] With Colombian peso continuing to strengthen against the dollar, chances of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  are increasing. "Chances that \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Colombia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  does something is perhaps 1 in 3, but rising to 50-50" if the COP break significantly below 1800/dollar, says Win Thin at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Brown Brothers Harriman\f28 \uc2 \f2 . BBH says it expects Colombia to use measures similar to Brazil's IOF tax, which was implemented last year. COP is top EM \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in 2010, gaining 14% on the dollar. (kejal.vyas@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 1849 GMT [Dow Jones] \uc2 Morgan Stanley\uc2  increased its 2010 growth outlook for Latin America to 6.2% from 5.8%, but still expects the same moderate pace of growth in 2011 of 4.0%. Still, MS cautions that the region is still influenced by external demand and global fears, such as weakening US growth. "Concerns could increase and should serve as warning to optimism in the region. It appears that the best growth is behind us," said the note, which stresses that Brazil is particularly at risk with the pace of activity moving from 9% to over 11% and then stalling out near zero in the second quarter. (riva.froymovich@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1819 GMT [Dow Jones] Bank of America-Merrill Lynch revises its EUR/USD forecast to 1.20 by the end of 2010, upward from its earlier forecast of 1.15. "The downward revision to the US growth outlook reinforces our bullish [dollar] view for the remainder of the year," BofA \uc2 Merrill Lynch\uc2  strategists said. Investors often turn to the safe-harbor dollar when they worry over global growth prospects. USD/JPY will fall to 79 by the end of 2010, the analysts said, revising their forecast from an original year-end target of 81. "Low US interest rates, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  demand and domestic exporter interest should put downward pressure" on the pair, BofA Merrill said.(bradley.davis@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1809 GMT [Dow Jones] \uc2 Moody's\uc2  says it hasn't changed \uc2 PG&E\uc2 's (PCG) bond ratings following Thursday's explosion of the company's natural gas pipeline in San Bruno, Calif., but the rating agency is closely watching the utility for signs that the explosion -- along with a recent report that found PCG performed shoddy customer service in its smart-meter rollout -- could hurt the utility's relationship with regulators as it seeks a $1B+ rate-hike. Shares off 1.8% at $43.44. (cassandra.sweet@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1806 GMT [Dow Jones] The pace of emerging market inflows picked up slightly last week, thanks to solid demand for Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , said Gareth Berry of \uc2 UBS\uc2 . The South Africa rand also attracted above-average buying volumes. However, the bank's book saw the Mexican peso sell against the dollar, and Berry said clients "showed a clear willingness to avoid over-exposing themselves to Eastern Europe."\par \par \uc2 (riva.froymovich@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1746 GMT [Dow Jones] Volume picks up a bit in some of the more closely-watched 2011 fed-funds futures contracts, as market reduces odds for FOMC to start lifting funds rate in 3Q next year. Oct '11 sees 60% chance for Fed to raise rate to 0.5% at meeting next Sept. Same contract priced in 76% chance at Fri's settlement. (howard.packowitz@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1737 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/CAD continues to probe the lower reaches of its recent range, notching a fresh session low at 1.0266, according to EBS via CQG. That's its lowest level since Aug 19. CAD remains strong despite the fact stocks and crude oil futures have trimmed their gains somewhat in recent trading. (don.curren@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1717 GMT [Dow Jones] Discover increases credit card receivables-backed ABS to $600M from $500M and launches at 58 bps over 1-month Libor. Should price later Mon.\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (anusha.shrivastava@dowjones.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1655 GMT [Dow Jones] It's unlikely Harrisburg will file for municipal bankruptcy, as championed by some city officials, especially with the governor and mayor against the option, says \f28 \uc2 \f2 Janney Montgomery Scott\f28 \uc2 \f2 's Alan Schankel. He notes the city is working on its $4.3M budget gap with cuts and increased fees. "A Chapter 9 filing would not magically eliminate the city's debt obligations," he writes. (romy.varghese@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1648 GMT [Dow Jones] Treasury prices higher across the board now as investors still worried about econ outlook take advantage of last week's price drop and come back in. Buying comes ahead of key retail sales report Tuesday morning and follows another Treasury purchase from the Fed Monday morning. 2-yr up 2/32 to 0.535%, 10-yr up 11/32 to 2.753% and 30-yr up 9/32 to yld 3.852%. (deborah.blumberg@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1642 GMT [Dow Jones] Volume for \f28 \uc2 \f2 CME Group\f28 \uc2 \f2 's core interest rate product line isn't so bad even though short-term rates aren't moving much from very low levels. Instead, traders shift to more volatile long-term rate futures, which generate higher rates per traded contract and better earnings, according to recently-released \f28 \uc2 \f2 JPMorgan\f28 \uc2 \f2  trade note. For example, Treasury futures lure investors seeking to "grab yield" before long-term rates presumably move lower. Tsy supplies sold at auction and uncertainty about the economic recovery also help to increase volatility. \f28 \uc2 \f2 JPMorgan\f28 \uc2 \f2  maintains overweight rating at 12-month target of $370. CME this morning hit 1-month top of $272.05. Recently 1.8% higher at $269.68. (howard.packowitz@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1630 GMT [Dow Jones] Long-term Tsy futures extend their rebound from overnight lows, with Dec 10-yr note futures very close to 2.75% cash yield equivalent. Dec 10-yrs climb to 123-26+. 2.75% equivalent pegged at 123-27, according to Optima Investment Research. Resistance also at Fri's high of 123-29. Dec 30-yr Tsy bonds rise to 130-18, with resistance at Fri's top of 131-01. (howard.packowitz@dowjones.com) [ 09-13-10 1455ET ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 4022   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020100913e69d000c0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw427\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal6405\pichgoal600
