\par\par \b \uc2 Colombian Stocks Climb 1.5% Tracking US Gains; Peso Weakens\b0\par\par\uc2 264 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 August 2010\par 21:17\par \uc2 Dow Jones News Service\par \uc2 DJ\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 CARTAGENA, Colombia (Dow Jones)--Colombian stocks moved higher Friday, boosted by the surge in U.S. markets, while the peso weakened slightly on expectations that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's appreciation.\par \par \uc2 The benchmark IGBC stock index rose 1.51% to 13,904 points. The index tracked the gains in New York, with the Dow Jones Industrial Average posting a midday increase of 125 points, or 1.3%, to 10,111 points on reassurances by Federal Reserve Chairman Ben Bernanke that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was ready to take actions to spur a faltering economic recovery.\par \par \uc2 In Colombia, shares of state oil firm \uc2 Ecopetrol SA\uc2  (ECOPETROL.BO) climbed 1.33% to COP3,435.\par \par \uc2 The peso, meanwhile, weakened slightly to COP1,817.4 from COP1,816 a day earlier. On Thursday, Finance Minister Juan Carlos Echeverry said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was "worried" by the appreciation of the peso, which has gained 11% against the dollar this year.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  didn't announce any plans last week to buy dollars in the spot market. The bank bought $1.6 billion in the first six months of the year in a bid to tame the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's appreciation. Some analysts believe that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could soon carry out similar \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the spot market.\par \par \uc2 The yield on \b \highlight22\uc2 Colombia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's benchmark 2020 bond stood at 7.130% compared to 7.179% a day earlier.\par \par \uc2 -By Darcy Crowe, Dow Jones Newswires; (58) 314 298 3277; darcy.crowe@dowjones.com [ 08-27-10 1517ET ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJ00000020100827e68r000gj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
