\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1- \highlight22\uc2 Colombia \highlight\uc2  peso falls, cenbank  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  expected\b0\par\par\uc2 309 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Oktober 2009\par 16:16\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited    \par \par \uc2 (Adds closing market level, analyst comment)\par \par \uc2 BOGOTA, Oct 27 (Reuters) - Colombia's peso weakened 1.7 percent on Tuesday as the U.S. dollar rallied around the world and the local market braced itself for the start of a series of dollar purchases that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  announced on Friday.\par \par \uc2 The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fell to 1,983 per dollar amid uncertainty about when the bank will start \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  and how much of its reserves it is willing to spend in its campaign to control the peso's strength.\par \par \uc2 "The lack of clarity obviously has people wondering," one local \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader said.\par \par \uc2 The bank on Friday said it plans to spend $1.5 billion by the end of the year on dollar purchases and buybacks of local TES treasury paper. But it did not provide a breakdown of how much would be spent on \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  versus buybacks.\par \par \uc2 The peso has rallied 19 percent against the dollar over the last 12 months, sparking howls from Colombian exporters who have been receiving rapidly weakening greenbacks for their international sales while paying costs in pesos.\par \par \uc2 Farmers and manufacturers are putting pressure on policymakers to do something about the strong local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Economists expect the peso to continue its strengthening trend despite the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy.\par \par \uc2 The dollar meanwhile rose to a two-week high against the euro on Tuesday after a report showing U.S. consumer confidence deteriorated sharply in October boosted the greenback's safe-haven appeal.\par \par \uc2 "The exchange rate in Colombia reacted mainly to the strength of the dollar in international markets," said analyst Julian Cardenas of Bogota-based brokerage Corredores Asociados. (Reporting by Nelson Bocanegra, writing by Hugh Bronstein, Editing by Chizu Nomiyama)\par \par \uc2 COLOMBIA-PESO/ (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|E|RBN|U|RNP|DNP    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020091027e5ar001oj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
